// ⭐⭐ **WHICH IMAGE-DATA RECORD A MODULE-LEVEL `let` IS — the three shapes, and the whole of what a
// materializing site cannot read off its own op.**
export union ImmortalRecordKind
	// The op's own bytes ARE the payload: a record in `.rdata` beside its immortal blob. A byte string and
	// a constant array literal both land here, and neither can carry a managed element
	// (`SignatureIndex.arrayElementMayBeConstantBlob`), so `element_destroy@40` is trivial by construction.
	constBlob

	// ⭐ An EMPTY `Array with T` — no payload, no blob, and the one shape whose ELEMENT TYPE still matters:
	// a clone off this record inherits `element_destroy@40` and then receives elements. `elementDestroy` is
	// the element's drop callee, `inert` when the element owns nothing.
	emptyContainer(elementDestroy OwnershipCallee)

	// ⭐⭐ **AN ARRAY OF STRING LITERALS — the one shape that is a TABLE OF ADDRESSES rather than of values.**
	// Its element buffer holds one pointer per element, each aimed at that element's own immortal `.rdata`
	// String record by a `GlobalDataTable.PendingRdataAbsReloc`; `texts` are the elements' decoded bytes, in
	// slot order, and each becomes such a record. `elementDestroy` is the String drop callee, carried for
	// `emptyContainer`'s reason — a clone off this record inherits `element_destroy@40` and may then receive
	// heap elements.
	//
	// ⚠ **IT NEVER APPEARS IN `ImmortalConstArraySiteMap` BELOW, BECAUSE IT IS A DIFFERENT OP.** A
	// `constArrayLiteral` carries ONE payload and serves an owned heap literal as well, so it needs the side
	// table to say which of the two a site is; a string table has no heap spelling and its payload is N
	// separate literals, so `Parser.emitImageRecordRead` emits `MaxonOp.immortalStringTable` for it and
	// `LowerMaxonToStd.lowerConstArrayLiteral` panics if this shape reaches the mark.
	stringTable(texts ByteArrayArray, elementDestroy OwnershipCallee)

	// ⭐⭐ **A DECLARED CONTAINER'S BOX — a `Map`/`Set` `let` whose `create()` is nothing but `Self{}`.**
	// `nodes` is the whole record tree and `root` names its outermost box; each node's `columns` name the
	// slots that hold its empty `Array` columns and its nested boxes, every one of which the lowering
	// registers as an image object of its own and addresses by an absolute data-to-data relocation.
	// `TopLevelImageRecord.bytes` carries nothing for this shape — a node's bytes are the node's.
	//
	// ⚠ **IT NEVER APPEARS IN `ImmortalConstArraySiteMap` BELOW**, for `stringTable`'s reason: its box is
	// not a `__ManagedMemory` record and no `constArrayLiteral` op can carry it.
	//
	// ⚠ Declared after `stringTable`.
	containerBox(nodes ImmortalBoxNodeArray, root ElementIndex)
end 'ImmortalRecordKind'

// @generated library-cache begin
function cacheWriteImmortalRecordKind(writer LibraryCacheWriter, value ImmortalRecordKind)
	writer.unsigned(value.ordinal as CacheUnsigned)

