	// ⭐ **THE INTERFACE NAMES THIS ENUM/UNION'S `implements` CLAUSE WRITES** — the exact twin of
	// `StructLayout.conformsTo`, which owns why the declaration sweep's copy is not the conformance
	// checker's record. It is the fact the abstract-`throws` narrowing reads
	// (`ConformanceCheck.requireImplErrorConformsAndIsScalar`): without it, `throws Error` would narrow to
	// ANY enum, including one that declares no conformance at all.
	//
	// ⚠ **THERE IS NO BINDINGS COLUMN BESIDE IT, and the asymmetry with `StructLayout` is deliberate.** The
	// `with` arguments ride the `ConformanceDecl` the real parse files, which is their only reader
	// (`checkConformance` substitutes them into a requirement); a conditional extension is expanded over
	// declared types alone (`ProgramSignatures.conformersOf`), so a column here would have nothing to answer.
